Context
  Asked for a wrapper that looks for the version and runs the eval once we bump past
  it. Issue #20 can be closed when it actually runs.

Deviations
  Version alone was not enough, so the wrapper does not stop there. The whole reason
  #20 exists is that I read a capability off --help and was wrong; a wrapper that
  trusted a version number would repeat that mistake in automated form. The probe is
  the authority and the version check is an early, free filter in front of it.

Considerations
  MIN_VERSION is a constant with a changelog citation rather than data in
  contracts/cell.json. cell.json records the environment the contracts were MEASURED
  on; 'the release that ships plugin eval' is a claim about the product, and mixing
  the two would make a version bump look like a contract re-measure.

  The probe case defaults to no-linter-claim because it has one grader and needs no
  REPL. If the gate opens and that case is removed, PROBE_CASE overrides it.

  Untested beyond the gated path: everything after the probe passes has never
  executed here. The flags are taken from --help on 2.1.261 and may have changed by
  2.1.269.

Timeline
  2026-09-29, nexus, claude-code-2.1.261 from pkg, as dsp-dr. Version comparison
  calibrated against six versions; end-to-end run verified on the gated path.
